  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0447, and it contains five tables. The first table, User, has the following columns: Associated_Unit, Password, Phone_Number, Role, User_ID (primary key), and Username. The second table, Financial_Document, has the following columns: Attachment_Path, Document_Category, Document_Content, Document_ID (primary key), Document_Level, Document_Number, Document_Title, Issue_Date, Issuing_Unit, Remarks, and Validity_Status. The third table, Notification, has the following columns: Issue_Date, Notification_Content, Notification_ID (primary key), Notification_Status, Notification_Title, and User_ID (foreign key referencing User.User_ID). The fourth table, System_Configuration, has the following columns: Admin_ID (foreign key referencing User.User_ID), Configuration_ID (primary key), Data_Type, Database_Directory, File_Upload_Directory, and System_Name. The fifth table, Document_Management, has the following columns: Admin_ID (foreign key referencing User.User_ID), Document_ID (foreign key referencing Financial_Document.Document_ID), Operation_Time, Operation_Type, and PRIMARY KEY (Admin_ID, Document_ID).",
  "gold_question": "Requirements:\n1.User Information Management: Each registered user in the financial system has a unique user ID, username, password, phone number, associated unit, and role.\n2.Financial Document Management: Collect and organize financial systems, accounting treatment FAQs, accounting practice tips, and other materials. Each financial document includes the document title, document number, issuing unit, issue date, document category, document level, validity status, remarks, document content, and attachment path. Administrators can perform operations on the document, recording the operation time and type.\n3.Notification Management: Users can publish notifications. The content of the notification includes the notification content, issue date, and notification status.\n4.Web System Configuration: Administrators can perform operations such as adding, modifying, or deleting database content. The configuration records the system name, database directory, data type, and file upload directory.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0447.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0447\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Role` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Associated_Unit` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Financial_Document` (\n  `Document_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Document_Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Document_Content` text NOT NULL,\n  `Document_Category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Document_Number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Document_Level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Issue_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Issuing_Unit` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Validity_Status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Document_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Notification` (\n  `Notification_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Notification_Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Notification_Content` text NOT NULL,\n  `Issue_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Notification_Status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Notification_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `System_Configuration` (\n  `Configuration_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Admin_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `System_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Data_Type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Database_Directory` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `File_Upload_Directory` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Configuration_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `System_Configuration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Admin_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Document_Management` (\n  `Admin_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Document_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Operation_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Operation_Type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Admin_ID`, `Document_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Document_Management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Admin_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Document_Management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Document_ID`) REFERENCES `Financial_Document` (`Document_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
